string_sculptor
===============

Write a function:

    def string_sculptor(text: str) -> str

Alternate the case of LETTERS in `text`: the 1st letter is lowercase,
the 2nd letter is uppercase, the 3rd letter is lowercase, and so on.

Non-letter characters are kept as-is AND do not advance the alternation
counter (so a space or digit does not "use up" a turn).

Examples:
    string_sculptor("Hello")     -> "hElLo"
    string_sculptor("ABCD")      -> "aBcD"
    string_sculptor("a b c d")   -> "a B c D"
    string_sculptor("12abc")     -> "12aBc"
